Day 27: A New Heart | Monday of the Fourth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“I will give you a new heart.”
Not patched.
Not repaired.
New.

Welcome to Day 27 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you into the deep, quiet work God longs to do within you — not surface change, not behavior modification, but inner renewal. A heart that is alive again. A heart that can feel again. A heart that responds to God with tenderness instead of resistance.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that God does not shame the hardened or weary places in you. He restores them — gently, faithfully, like a surgeon with steady hands. A new heart is not something you earn; it is something you receive.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why God promises renewal, not repair

How Lent becomes a season of inner transformation

What a “new heart” looks like in daily life

A prayer for renewal and openness

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, renew my heart.”

